  "function": {
    "uniprot_function": "Constitutively active serine/threonine-protein kinase that acts as a negative regulator in multiple signaling pathways including Wnt, Hedgehog, PI3K-AKT, and circadian clock. Phosphorylates and inactivates glycogen synthase (GYS1), thereby regulating glycogen synthesis. Phosphorylates numerous transcription factors and signaling proteins, typically priming them for ubiquitin-mediated degradation. Key regulator of cell fate determination, embryonic development, and cell proliferation. Phosphorylates beta-catenin (CTNNB1), leading to its degradation in absence of Wnt signaling. Phosphorylates tumor suppressors APC and AXIN1. Involved in energy metabolism, neuronal cell development, and body pattern formation.",
    "catalytic_activity": "ATP + [protein]-L-serine = ADP + [protein]-L-serine phosphate (EC 2.7.11.26). Preferentially phosphorylates substrates that have been primed by prior phosphorylation (phosphate-primed substrates).",
