    "pathway_role_summary": "GSK3B is a central negative regulator in multiple signaling pathways. In Wnt signaling, it phosphorylates beta-catenin for degradation when Wnt is absent. Upon Wnt activation, GSK3B is inhibited, allowing beta-catenin stabilization. In PI3K-AKT signaling, AKT phosphorylates and inhibits GSK3B in response to insulin and growth factors. GSK3B also regulates Hedgehog signaling by phosphorylating GLI transcription factors, controls circadian rhythms through BMAL1/CLOCK phosphorylation, and contributes to neurodegeneration through tau hyperphosphorylation."
  },
