    "data_quality_notes": "High quality data from multiple sources. Extensive structural data available (>100 PDB structures). Comprehensive interaction data from multiple databases. Kinetic parameters available for some interactions (AKT-GSK3B, GSK3B-CTNNB1, Axin-GSK3B, LRP6-GSK3B) but many interactions lack quantitative binding/kinetic data. PTM data comprehensive for phosphorylation but limited for other modification types. Disease associations well-documented for neurodegenerative diseases and diabetes.",
    "modeling_relevance_summary": "GSK3B is critical for Wnt pathway modeling as the key kinase in the beta-catenin destruction complex. Its dual regulation (inhibitory Ser9 phosphorylation by AKT, activating Tyr216 autophosphorylation) and dramatic activity enhancement by Axin scaffold (>20000-fold) are essential for quantitative modeling. The priming phosphate requirement (R96 site) explains substrate specificity. Available kinetic data (KD values for Axin binding ~35 \u03bcM, LRP6 inhibition Ki ~13 \u03bcM, phosphorylation rates) enable mechanistic modeling of Wnt pathway dynamics. Over 100 crystal structures provide detailed structural information for molecular modeling."
